Covalent-geometry restraint data
================================

Two data sets, both from the Phenix/cctbx project and both under the BSD-3-style LBNL licence
reproduced below.

1. cdl_v1_2.f32 -- Conformation-Dependent Library v1.2
------------------------------------------------------

Backbone bond-length and bond-angle targets and esds as a function of the residue's phi/psi
(Moriarty, Tronrud, Adams & Karplus 2014, FEBS J 281:4061, doi:10.1111/febs.12860; Berkholz,
Shapovalov, Dunbrack & Karplus 2009, Structure 17:1316, doi:10.1016/j.str.2009.08.012).

Format: little-endian f32, 8 residue classes x 36 phi bins x 36 psi bins x 24 values.
  Classes, in order: NonPGIV_nonxpro, IleVal_nonxpro, Gly_nonxpro, Pro_nonxpro,
                     NonPGIV_xpro, IleVal_xpro, Gly_xpro, Pro_xpro
  Bins: phi and psi from -180 to 170 in steps of 10 (the cctbx dictionary keys).
  Values: (target, esd) for C(-1)-N-CA, N-CA-CB, N-CA-C, CB-CA-C, CA-C-O, CA-C-N(+1),
          O-C-N(+1), C(-1)-N, N-CA, CA-CB, CA-C, C-O. A target of -1 marks a term the class
          lacks (the CB terms of glycine).

Source: cctbx_project mmtbx/conformation_dependent_library/cdl_database.py ("CDL v1.2",
git blob 9b5b41af00e9ba1013d6afbb1fb3ad6b55e708a1), as shipped in cctbx-base 2025.11.
Generated by scripts/convert_geostd.py.

2. src/geometry/library.rs -- heavy-atom restraints of the 20 amino acids and MSE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bond, angle, chirality and planarity restraints of the monomers ALA ... VAL and MSE, the
TRANS and PTRANS peptide links and the C-terminal COO modification, from Phenix geostd
(the geostd monomer files state they are copies of the CCP4 monomer library entries of the
time, i.e. Engh & Huber 1991 values; Acta Cryst A47:392, doi:10.1107/S0108767391001071).
Restraints involving hydrogen are dropped. Chirality ideal volumes are computed by cctbx from
each monomer's own ideal bonds and angles, as pdb_interpretation does.

Source: https://github.com/phenix-project/geostd, commit
4e1c1c0444d9ab9c4a1e01626011ea0f62fddb16 (2026-09-15), files <letter>/data_<RES>.cif and
list/mon_lib_list.cif, read through the cctbx monomer-library server. Generated by
scripts/convert_geostd.py.

Evaluation (which restraints exist, the CDL and cis-proline rules, symmetric-atom flips, the
4-sigma outlier rules) replicates cctbx pdb_interpretation, conformation_dependent_library
and mmtbx/validation/restraints.py; crates/proteus-core/tests/geometry_validation.rs checks
the result against cctbx structure by structure.

